  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">DPASI now has the capability to transport members and persons with disabilities to attend activities, training and events, support its advocacy and support efforts across Honiara and Guadalcanal, using a dedicated vehicle, funded under Australia&#x2019;s Civil Society Strengthening Program (SICSSP).</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">IWDA support to FSC and CCC has enabled more women in Solomon Islands to access shelter and counselling services.  With FSC&#x2019;s continual provincial awareness programs, client increases have been noticed in Tulagi (over 600%) and Kirakira (nearly 300%).</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Women&#x2019;s Development Agency and UN Women Pacific Partnership support to Family support Centre (FSC) and Christian Care Centre (CCC) has enabled more women in the Solomon Islands to access shelter and counselling services through CCC and FSC. The FSC branch opening in Gizo has increased and improved provincial service provision and impacted on the number of women and girls to access GBV services and have access to qualified counsellors, legal advice, and case management..</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under Post&apos;s bilateral aid program, DFAT funded IWDA to support WRAM and the Ministry of Women, Youth, Children &amp; Family Affairs&#x2019; (MWYCFA&#x2019;s) Women Development Division (WDD) in the Women Ignite Stability and Economic Recovery (WISER) project.  Nation-wide TSM awareness was the major activity.  Several communities in all nine provinces, together with Honiara city, were reached.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
